<title>FRANCE: Lowest French wheat bid seen covering 20,000 T.</title>
<headline>Lowest French wheat bid seen covering 20,000 T.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The lowest rebate offer of 13.95 Ecus per tonne placed through France is for the export of up to 20,000 tonnes of European Union soft wheat, grain traders estimated on Thursday.</p>
<p>In France exporters bid at this week's EU tender to ship a total of 483,000 tonnes of free-market soft wheat at refunds ranging from 13.95 to 18.57 Ecus per tonne, grain office ONIC reported earlier.</p>
<p>French wheat bids included up to 117,000 tonnes of soft wheat at a maximum refund of 14.50 Ecus per tonne, up to 257,000 tonnes at 15.50 Ecus, and up to 403,000 tonnes at 16.00 Ecus.</p>
<p>Last week the European Union granted the export of 71,900 tonnes of free-market soft wheat at a maximum rebate of 14.50 Ecus per tonne.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
